    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **32 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in the owner creation flow (`POST /api/owners`), handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`:\n\n- Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`:\n  ```java\n  private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n  ```\n- After the owner is successfully saved, it emits one audit line carrying the three required fields:\n  ```java\n  AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nThe line is emitted only after `saveOwner` succeeds (so it reflects the assigned id and generated `customerCode`), and it uses the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` that is stored on the owner \u2014 matching what the test reads back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The new `Cp21Tests` passes and no existing tests regressed.",
